#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0605 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "MECHANISM PIN (Fix #269 / EC-84) - the shape that USED TO CRASH the run. Rows 1 and 3 carry a populated APHASEN, row 2 is blank, so the leading `not empty(APHASEN)` never empties the mask and compileAnd reaches the substituted comparison; Primitives.scan then resolves the RHS for EVERY row, including row 2. Before Fix #269 that row threw OperandSubstitutor.SubstitutionException out through RuleRunner (a JUnit ERROR, not a verdict). Now the unresolvable substitution is `no value` for that row, the rule evaluates, and only row 3 (APHASEN=2 -> ADSL.PH2SDT=23100, PHSDT 23900 != 23100) fires. Row 1 matches (23000 == PH1SDT). Row 2 is silent because the rule's own `not empty(APHASEN)` guard excludes it - the per-row `no value` is not, by itself, a suppression."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 APHASEN=2 PHSDT=23900
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col AVAL     type=Num
col APHASEN  type=Num
col PHSDT    type=Num
---
S1 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 30 | 1 | 23000
S1 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | 31 | . | 23500
S1 | 01-701-1031 | ALB | 32 | 2 | 23900
---

dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PH1SDT  type=Num
col PH2SDT  type=Num
---
S1 | 01-701-1015 | 23000 | 23100
S1 | 01-701-1023 | 23000 | 23100
S1 | 01-701-1031 | 23000 | 23100
